[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-complexion@68961e61bd0355ff3bf7a5f61a0e68916a5d8424/docs/img/groups.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][size=4][b]In Fallout 4, almost everyone has the same clean, blank skin. Complexion gives every NPC a look of their own the first time you meet them: tattoos, scars, moles, grime and more, chosen for who they are. Raiders are inked and scarred, settlers mostly plain.[/b][/size][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#e0a85a]In short[/color][/b][/size]

[b]What you get[/b]
[list]
[*]Every NPC gets skin overlays when you first meet them, and keeps them: tattoos, scars, moles, freckles, body hair, bruises, grime.[/*]
[*]The look fits the person: twelve faction groups (raiders, Gunners, the Brotherhood, the Institute and more), each with its own style.[/*]
[*]59 named characters have their own look from their stories: Cait, Piper, Danse, Fahrenheit and others.[/*]
[*]A window in game to pick overlays by hand, for anyone or for yourself, with a live preview.[/*]
[/list][b]What you need[/b]: F4SE, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394]Runtime Database[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/12631]LooksMenu[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/21497]MCM[/url]. Overlay packs are optional: Complexion paints 699 of its own.
[b]Supported bodies[/b]: CBBE or CBBE 3BBB for women, any BodySlide preset (the shape changes, the UV map does not); the vanilla male body or BodyTalk for men. The vanilla female body is NOT supported: its UV map differs from CBBE's, so the overlays land in the wrong places (stray rectangles and outlines).
[b]How it goes[/b]: install with Vortex or MO2, load your save, and meet people. Using Random Overlay Framework? Read [b]Moving from Random Overlay Framework[/b] below first: you may keep it.

[size=5][b][color=#e0a85a]What it is[/color][/b][/size]

Complexion is the replacement for Random Overlay Framework. It uses LooksMenu's overlays, the same system tattoo and skin-detail packs use, and decides for each person which ones they get. It decides once per person, when you first meet them, and the look stays. There is no constant scanning in the background.

Never more than six overlays on anyone, one style per person, never three of a kind, no two tattoos on one spot, and a faction's emblem only on its own people. Pieces that break the lore (superheroes, real brands) and poor-quality ones are never handed out.

[b]How it works:[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6687]Complexion - under the hood →[/url]

[size=5][b][color=#e0a85a]What you get[/color][/b][/size]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-complexion@68961e61bd0355ff3bf7a5f61a0e68916a5d8424/docs/img/composition.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]One look, not a pile.[/b] At most six overlays, one style, never three of a kind, no two tattoos on one spot.[/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-complexion@68961e61bd0355ff3bf7a5f61a0e68916a5d8424/docs/img/characters.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]The named people.[/b] 59 characters get a look from their stories: Cait scarred from the Combat Zone, Piper all but plain, Danse under the Brotherhood's mark, Fahrenheit inked.[/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-complexion@68961e61bd0355ff3bf7a5f61a0e68916a5d8424/docs/img/marks.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Its own marks.[/b] 699 overlays painted for Complexion, for the CBBE and male bodies: moles, freckles, birthmarks, stretch marks, body and pubic hair, tan lines, scars of every kind, classic flash tattoos, bruises, grime and blood. Each one fades out before the neck and wrist seams.[/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-complexion@68961e61bd0355ff3bf7a5f61a0e68916a5d8424/docs/img/window.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Choose by hand.[/b] Aim at anyone, or at no one for yourself, and press the window's hotkey (set it in MCM > Complexion). They stand still, undressed, and the window lists every overlay that fits them, by category, with a search. A click puts one on, live, and the camera goes to where it sits. Random rolls a look, Apply keeps it, Cancel puts back what they had, clothes included. This is how you get overlays on your own character: you are never given a random look.[/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-complexion@68961e61bd0355ff3bf7a5f61a0e68916a5d8424/docs/img/packs.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Your packs too.[/b] Overlay packs are optional. Complexion includes no other author's overlays, but it hands out the ones you have installed alongside its own: about 1,900 overlays of 16 popular packs are sorted from their pictures. A pack it does not know is left alone.[/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-complexion@68961e61bd0355ff3bf7a5f61a0e68916a5d8424/docs/img/cheap.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Light, and kind to other mods.[/b] One decision per person and one rebuild, ever: no cloak spell, no waiting, no faction scans in scripts. Overlays other mods put on someone (AAF, Rapport) are kept and drawn on top. Nobody is touched during an AAF scene, and the player, the dead and children never are.[/center]

[size=5][b][color=#e0a85a]Install[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Install with Vortex or MO2; installing by hand is not supported.[/b] The installer first checks your setup and will not run without LooksMenu. Complexion checks the rest in game and tells you what is missing.

[b]Moving from Random Overlay Framework[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Using its tattoo packs? Keep Random Overlay Framework (Invictusblade's packs need its plugin) and install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/69798]RobCo Patcher[/url]: Complexion then switches ROF's handing-out off, without touching its files or your save, and tells you in game if it could not. Not using its packs? Uninstall it.[/*]
[*]Load your save and press MCM > Complexion > [i]Clear every overlay[/i] once, outside any AAF scene.[/*]
[*]Save and load. Complexion gives people their looks again as you meet them.[/*]
[/list][quote]
[b]Needs:[/b] Fallout 4 1.10.163 (old-gen), 1.10.984 (next-gen) or 1.11.x (Anniversary Edition), F4SE, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394]Runtime Database[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/12631]LooksMenu[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/21497]MCM[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/15]CBBE[/url] or CBBE 3BBB for women's overlays.
[b]Optional:[/b] LooksMenu overlay packs. Complexion paints its own and hands out the packs you have alongside. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/69798]RobCo Patcher[/url], only if you keep Random Overlay Framework.[/quote][size=5][b][color=#e0a85a]Incompatibilities[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Random Overlay Framework without RobCo Patcher[/b]: both would hand out overlays. Install RobCo Patcher so Complexion can switch ROF's handing-out off, or uninstall ROF (see above).[/*]
[/list][size=5][b][color=#e0a85a]FAQ[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Which bodies?[/b]
[spoiler]CBBE or CBBE 3BBB for women, any BodySlide preset (the shape changes, the UV map does not); the vanilla male body or BodyTalk for men. The vanilla female body is NOT supported: its UV map differs from CBBE's, so the overlays land in the wrong places (stray rectangles and outlines).[/spoiler]

[b]Why did someone's overlays change after updating?[/b]
[spoiler]Their body hair was another colour than the hair on their head, so Complexion chose their look again, once. Looks you picked in the overlay window are never changed.[/spoiler]

[b]Do I need overlay packs?[/b]
[spoiler]No. Complexion paints 699 overlays of its own. If you have LooksMenu overlay packs installed, it hands out the ones it knows alongside its own.[/spoiler]

[b]Will it change my own character?[/b]
[spoiler]Only if you ask it to. You are never given a random look; the overlay window is how you put overlays on yourself.[/spoiler]

[b]Do I need AAF?[/b]
[spoiler]No. With AAF, Complexion waits until a scene is over and keeps AAF's own overlays. Without it, everything works.[/spoiler]

[b]Where are the settings?[/b]
[spoiler]MCM, page "Complexion": the window's hotkey, the switches, and the buttons (including "Clear every overlay").[/spoiler]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-anatomy@497c254d44fa1fc28df6db8fe1fb50269bb6e963/docs/img/divider.png[/img][/center]

Complexion.dll is [url=https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/dba49e9d86a94d80cef8adacb1a743f315c28cbd31a1d72f62e773a354b819cc]clean on VirusTotal[/url] (0/75). Source: [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-complexion]GitHub[/url], GPL-3.0.

